{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/273627-has-anyone-done-a-scion-conversion-for-wod","id":273627,"title":"Has anyone done a scion conversion for WoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-06T05:13:26-07:00","id":273627,"title":"Has anyone done a scion conversion for WoD?","content":"Was just thinking about this today.<br /> <br /> Just some minor things like this:<br /> <br /> Scions are the children of humans and a spirit which is the incarnation of a story. <br /> <br /> Calling, every scion has a calling that they are pursuing. They are usually heroic in nature, but just as often heroic in the old world myth sense as in a modern one. And old world heroes would often be considered a villain in modern times. The only thing that they have in common is that their callings are worthy of sagas.<br /> <br /> Reduce Epics to adding +1 dice per level rather than +1, +2, +4, +7, +11 and so on successes.<br /> <br /> Have factions like this:<br /> <br /> Tall Tales - It is stories that empower a scion and these scions want to make the biggest story possible. If possible, they prefer that their names are attached the stories told about them, believing it brings them power faster. However, it also brings them into more danger. They sometimes care about power more than their calling. Other times they don't particularly think about anything, but are just recklessly enjoying their power.<br /> <br /> Urban Legends - These scions create a story around themselves based on an archetype or other identity other than their real name. Like all scions, it is the story that brings them power, but they'd rather be the mysterious singer who appears at some venues, sings inhumanly beautiful songs and vanishes than the major rock star...or the lone hunter spoken of in the circles of those men and women who hunt the monsters. They are subtle and hard to track. In general, urban legends care more about safety than anything. Others think that the added mystery will cause their story to spread further.<br /> <br /> Paragons - These scions do not try to either exaggerate their stories or build up a mystery around themselves. They simply pursue their callings in the most efficient way possible and just let the story spread as far as it will naturally. The calling is often the most important aspect of their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stereotypes:<br /> Vampires: Stories about blood-drinking monsters have spread for as long as humans have been around. Maybe these creatures are a dark cousin of our own kind.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Half-spirit and half-flesh just like us, but they seem stuck on a unified story rather than following each their own path.<br /> <br /> Mages: So this is what happens when mortals learn about Fate? This could make us obsolete...or create an entirely new enemy for us to fight.<br /> <br /> Changelings: They remind me of some of the Titanspawn, stolen mortals corrupted by an inhuman and alien force. Which makes me remember just how few titan-corrupted mortals ever truly recover their soul and free will.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: Their geists feel very much like titan-corrupted specters. Just how much can we trust them?<br /> <br /> Demons: This monstrous machine sounds like an aspect of Prometheus and his mad obsession with technology. Are these actually turned titanspawn like the dwarves?<br /> <br /> Prometheans: They seem to tear apart everything around them slowly but surely. I suspect they're a poor job by some ancient cousin...or maybe something the titans have slipped into the world. Certainly some of them seem mad enough for that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T22:19:00-07:00","id":274500,"title":"","content":"I don't know about a full on conversion, but I once read a fanfic where Scion is in the same universe as the old World of Darkness. A newly ascended Sun Scion crashes into a building where the Camarilla are gathering, only to be attacked by a pack of Sabbat. The goddess obliterates the Sabbat with zero effort, much to the horror of the Camarilla witnesses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T00:35:44-07:00","id":274532,"title":"","content":"Don't doubt it, scions early on are more powerful than most of the OWoD templates but less than most Exalted. A full Legend 12 character makes Exalted look low-powered.<br /> <br /> Heck, anything Legend 9 or higher is basically a case of &quot;why do we have rules anymore?&quot;<br /> <br /> Everything at that level is like Cthulhu battling Hastur....you have to by fighting things on the conceptual level at that point, the physical is just a stalemate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T05:37:27-07:00","id":274655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/273627-has-anyone-done-a-scion-conversion-for-wod?p=274500#post274500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about a full on conversion, but I once read a fanfic where Scion is in the same universe as the old World of Darkness. A newly ascended Sun Scion crashes into a building where the Camarilla are gathering, only to be attacked by a pack of Sabbat. The goddess obliterates the Sabbat with zero effort, much to the horror of the Camarilla witnesses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds right to me.<br /> I mean it would sound very wrong if a sun scion at even a demigod level had much of a problem dealing with creatures that have a fatal allergy to sunlight. (Regardless of whatever blood magic or such that protects a parasite, a scion that is intimate with the sun should be able to blast a hole through it, or at least that's how I'd have it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:40:26-07:00","id":285909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/273627-has-anyone-done-a-scion-conversion-for-wod?p=274532#post274532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't doubt it, scions early on are more powerful than most of the OWoD templates but less than most Exalted. A full Legend 12 character makes Exalted look low-powered.<br /> <br /> Heck, anything Legend 9 or higher is basically a case of &quot;why do we have rules anymore?&quot;<br /> <br /> Everything at that level is like Cthulhu battling Hastur....you have to by fighting things on the conceptual level at that point, the physical is just a stalemate.</div> </div> </div> </div>At god or higher or perhaps even demigod, the Scion's peers would be beings like Archmages, Kerberoi or even Luna and True Fae at the extreme end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T18:35:04-07:00","id":286286,"title":"","content":"This is true, so a conversion would have to have them somewhat more limited...however, did get given one a friend made...haven't looked at it yet though.<br /> <br /> But yeah, high level Scion makes even Exalted look reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T19:56:48-07:00","id":286333,"title":"","content":"...when dealing with gods, one should be dealing with the highest levels of power in any game I should think. A god of magic should fear no archmage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:13:45-07:00","id":286337,"title":"","content":"I'd think in a NWoD setting, Scions would have more limited power and be more directly related to facet of Fate that is humanity's desire for great stories","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}